  "title": "Top 10 Things to Do in Phuket Old Town",
  "content": "<p>Phuket Old Town is a treasure trove of cultural heritage, stunning architecture, and authentic Thai experiences. Here are the top 10 things you must do when visiting this charming district.</p><h2>1. Walk Along Thalang Road</h2><p>The most iconic street in Old Town, Thalang Road showcases the best of Sino-Portuguese architecture. The colorful shophouses dating back to the 19th century create a perfect backdrop for photos.</p><figure><img src=\"/images/blog/top-10-things-to-do-in-phuket-old-town/soi-rommanee.webp\" alt=\"Soi Rommanee and its pastel shophouses at the Thalang Road junction\" width=\"1440\" height=\"813\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Soi Rommanee offers another view of Old Town’s colourful shophouses, just off Thalang Road.</figcaption></figure><h2>2. Visit the Sunday Walking Street Market</h2><p>Every Sunday evening, Thalang Road transforms into a vibrant night market. Sample local street food, shop for handicrafts, and enjoy live performances.</p><figure><img src=\"/images/blog/top-10-things-to-do-in-phuket-old-town/thalang-sunday-market.webp\" alt=\"Blue-canopied food stall at the Thalang Road Sunday market in Phuket Old Town\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1078\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>A Thalang Road market scene, with food stalls beneath blue canopies.</figcaption></figure><h2>3. Explore the Shrine of Serene Light</h2><p>This beautiful Chinese shrine, hidden down a narrow alley, offers a peaceful retreat from the bustling streets.</p><h2>4. Discover Street Art</h2><p>Phuket Old Town is home to numerous stunning murals and street art pieces that tell stories of local culture and history.</p><figure><img src=\"/images/blog/top-10-things-to-do-in-phuket-old-town/old-town-street-art.webp\" alt=\"Murals on buildings in Phuket Old Town\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1078\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Street art adds another layer to Phuket Old Town’s streets and buildings.</figcaption></figure><h2>5. Try Local Coffee Shops</h2><p>The area is dotted with charming cafes housed in restored shophouses, perfect for a relaxing afternoon break.</p><figure><img src=\"/images/blog/top-10-things-to-do-in-phuket-old-town/old-town-cafe.webp\" alt=\"Kopitiam by Wilai storefront and outdoor tables in Phuket Old Town at night\" width=\"1440\" height=\"960\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>A shophouse café scene at Kopitiam by Wilai in Phuket Old Town.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>If you are deciding whether town exploration should shape your hotel base, read our <a href=\"/phuket-town-or-patong\">Phuket Town or Patong stay guide</a> for the city and beach itinerary tradeoffs.</p>\n<p><small>Image credits: images are AI adaptations of location photographs, with fictional people. Thalang Road and Soi Rommanee by Slleong (<a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thalang_Road_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thalang Road source</a>; <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soi_Rommanee_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Soi Rommanee source</a>), <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CC0 1.0</a>. Market and murals by Christophe95 (<a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Phuket_Weekend_Market_03.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">market source</a>; <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Murals_in_Phuket_Town.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">mural source</a>); both adapted images are licensed <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kopitiam_by_Wilai,_Phuket_(13271249955).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kopitiam by Wilai source</a> by Thanakrit Gu, <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CC BY 2.0</a>.</small></p>",
